      "id": "coa-original-io-interface-programmed-interrupt",
      "verified": "BEU Exam Answer · 7 Marks",
      "intro": "The I/O interface adapts the system bus to a peripheral. Program-controlled and interrupt-driven I/O use its registers but differ in how the CPU learns that service is needed.",
